  </worksheets>
  <dashboards>
    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='How to use it?'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/BrandItemsRecommendations/Howtouseit?rev=' id='Howtouseit' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/ItemsRecommendationsGlossary' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='650' maxwidth='1000' minheight='650' minwidth='1000' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97538' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1231'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='18'>Items Recommendations Glossary</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>Data source:</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='12'>An internal statistical model that checks all brands in the entity and their dish items (with quantities sold &amp; frequencies in the last 30 days orders) and norm dish taxonomy data. The model establishes similarity between the brands based on the dish item vectors, and eventually recommends dish items from the similar brands that are not present in the Kitchen Brands’ menu.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>KPIs</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Item relevance rank</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>: How relevant is the recommended item to the current menu of the brand. Since this is ‘rank’, lower the value, higher the relevance; the most relevant item rank is 1.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Item price eur entity</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>: Average item price in euro in the entity.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Expected Revenue Uplift</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>: We estimate expected revenue uplift based on that item’s average revenue share in the similar competitors that are selling this item.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>Important Notes</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>1. There is </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>no correlation</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> between </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>item relevance rank</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> and </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>expected revenue uplift</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>. These are 2 different options that we provide:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>         &gt;  Some items are more associated with the brand&apos;s current menu items (item relevance rank). Here `associated` means that these items are more often sold by other similar brands, but not in the kitchen brand&apos;s menu. So they are probably easier to add, since many similar brands sell them.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>      &gt; Some items, (regardless of relevance with our brands current menu items) are sold by other similar brands (maybe only few of the relevant competitors sell), but these items bring a relatively good portion of the revenue for those brands who sell that item..</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='18'>!</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Manual review is required  to evaluate the worthiness of recommended items against its actual feasibility and expected value it can bring.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>2. </run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>What&apos;s the difference between relevant competitor area and relevant competitor entity in this report?</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> &gt;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Currently we have added top 3 relevant competitors in the area and top 3 relevant competitors in the entity. That could be exactly the same lists or may vary one from another in case there are some strong brands that only operate in the specific areas e.g., but are not that strong on entity level.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>3. </run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Due to the dish item standardization stage, (although not very frequent) there are some cases where the actual dish items may be misclassified, which is inevitably inherited from the norm dish taxonomy data. In such cases, the misclassification errors may have an impact on the quality of the recommendation results such as; mismatch between the referenced sample item and recommended item or even brands’ relevant competitors (relatively more rare).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>4. </run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Note that the referenced items are provided as a </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>sample</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> from a geographically nearby &amp; similar brand,</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> among many other similar brands.</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> The purpose is to give a showcase for the recommended item about what it looks like or how it is presented/styled in a similar brand in reality as an example, and not to copy the exact same referenced item, since the options are not limited to the sample references provided. So, during the evaluation, it is suggested to try imagining the potential ways to style &amp; adapt the recommended dish items to the style of our brand.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='18'>!</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>It should be noted that the intent of the item recommendations are to provide inspirations backed up with data as well as speeding up the manual decision-making process, and not to replace the human evaluation completely. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>Feedback</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>In case of any feedback or questions on this dashboard, please reach out on Slack to gfs-kitchen-data</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='14' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='97538' id='13' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1231'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97538' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1231'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='18'>Items Recommendations Glossary</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>Data source:</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='12'>An internal statistical model that checks all brands in the entity and their dish items (with quantities sold &amp; frequencies in the last 30 days orders) and norm dish taxonomy data. The model establishes similarity between the brands based on the dish item vectors, and eventually recommends dish items from the similar brands that are not present in the Kitchen Brands’ menu.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>KPIs</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Item relevance rank</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>: How relevant is the recommended item to the current menu of the brand. Since this is ‘rank’, lower the value, higher the relevance; the most relevant item rank is 1.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Item price eur entity</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>: Average item price in euro in the entity.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Expected Revenue Uplift</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>: We estimate expected revenue uplift based on that item’s average revenue share in the similar competitors that are selling this item.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>Important Notes</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>1. There is </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>no correlation</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> between </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>item relevance rank</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>expected revenue uplift</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>. These are 2 different options that we provide:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>         &gt;  Some items are more associated with the brand&apos;s current menu items (item relevance rank). Here `associated` means that these items are more often sold by other similar brands, but not in the kitchen brand&apos;s menu. So they are probably easier to add, since many similar brands sell them.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>      &gt; Some items, (regardless of relevance with our brands current menu items) are sold by other similar brands (maybe only few of the relevant competitors sell), but these items bring a relatively good portion of the revenue for those brands who sell that item..</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='18'>!</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Manual review is required  to evaluate the worthiness of recommended items against its actual feasibility and expected value it can bring.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>2. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>What&apos;s the difference between relevant competitor area and relevant competitor entity in this report?</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> &gt;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Currently we have added top 3 relevant competitors in the area and top 3 relevant competitors in the entity. That could be exactly the same lists or may vary one from another in case there are some strong brands that only operate in the specific areas e.g., but are not that strong on entity level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>3. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Due to the dish item standardization stage, (although not very frequent) there are some cases where the actual dish items may be misclassified, which is inevitably inherited from the norm dish taxonomy data. In such cases, the misclassification errors may have an impact on the quality of the recommendation results such as; mismatch between the referenced sample item and recommended item or even brands’ relevant competitors (relatively more rare).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>4. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Note that the referenced items are provided as a </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>sample</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> from a geographically nearby &amp; similar brand,</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> among many other similar brands.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> The purpose is to give a showcase for the recommended item about what it looks like or how it is presented/styled in a similar brand in reality as an example, and not to copy the exact same referenced item, since the options are not limited to the sample references provided. So, during the evaluation, it is suggested to try imagining the potential ways to style &amp; adapt the recommended dish items to the style of our brand.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='18'>!</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>It should be noted that the intent of the item recommendations are to provide inspirations backed up with data as well as speeding up the manual decision-making process, and not to replace the human evaluation completely. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9150c' fontsize='12'>Feedback</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>In case of any feedback or questions on this dashboard, please reach out on Slack to gfs-kitchen-data</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{CE3BDB5F-DAF2-48A4-88C6-A3BEC6F837E7}' />
